Message-4.text:
I've updated the canvas with a comprehensive color palette example using CSS variables. You can define your colors once in the :root selector like this:

:root {
  --primary-100: #e3f2fd;
  --primary-500: #2196f3;
  --primary-900: #0d47a1;
}

Then use them throughout your CSS with var(--primary-500) for your main brand color, var(--primary-100) for lighter variants, and var(--primary-900) for darker accents. This makes it much easier to maintain a consistent color scheme and update colors globally when needed.

